\begin_layout Title
Gravity, Trade and Transport
\end_layout

\begin_layout Author
Victor H. Aguiar
\end_layout

\begin_layout Date
ECON 803, Fall 2026
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Questions only. Restored from both parts of the SFU December 2024 final: the structural gravity argument and the Arabasta and Baltigo modeling case. Each question separates hand work from Codex and verification. Timing refers to the hand work. The original contraction request and the counterfactual income closure are corrected explicitly.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
These are the same questions as the textbook. Begin with the hand calculations and state a solution plan before using tools. Report the economic assumptions, the hand seed, one scaling step and an exact verification command. Numerical output alone is not a proof.
\end_layout

